.TH SSH-AUTH-SUMMARY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-auth-summary \- count offline OpenSSH server authentication message patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-auth-summary
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarize recognized sshd authentication message patterns within finite,
RFC3164-like local syslog text, with or without a numeric leading PRI.
This is a bounded, read-only log-message analysis, not a security verdict,
a source of genuine unique logins or a guarantee of log completeness.
No messages, identities, addresses, hostnames or input paths are emitted.
Other programs and host log files are not accessed implicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read an ordinary file without following symlinks, or stdin (default).
.TP
.B --null
Emit seven pairs of NUL-terminated EVENT/COUNT fields without a heading.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage on standard output.
.TP
.B --version
Print the command and version.
.SH OUTPUT
TSV columns EVENT and COUNT with rows ACCEPTED, FAILED, INVALID_USER,
OTHER_SSHD, OTHER_SERVICE, UNKNOWN, TOTAL. The first three are recognized
OpenSSH message patterns; they do not count unique authentication attempts.
No personal identifiers or raw log lines are shown.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All input envelopes structurally recognized, or empty input.
.TP
.B 1
At least one envelope was UNKNOWN; no other input failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Source unavailable, symlink, invalid framing, incomplete LF-terminated
input, or resource limits exceeded. No partial report.
.SH LIMITS
At most 16 MiB, 128 KiB per physical line, 50,000 records. Accepts LF and
CRLF. Does not follow live streams, parse RFC5424 or native macOS Unified
Logging, handle rotations, or query PAM, sudo or SSH itself.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B printf '%s\\n' 'Oct 21 08:30:04 host sshd[1]: Invalid user test from 192.0.2.1 port 22' | ssh-auth-summary
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syslog-summary (1),
.BR journal-summary (1),
.BR login-audit (1)
